{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1777738235986,"sessionID":"ses_2168e1f72ffejDHysUaUdBXqdN","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_6c138b10b7ac47c895f18e16","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/work/push_swap.rs","content":"fn parse_args(args: Vec<String>) -> Result<Vec<i32>, ()> {\n    let mut nums: Vec<i32> = Vec::new();\n    for arg in args.iter().skip(1) {\n        if arg.is_empty() {\n            return Err(());\n        }\n        for tok in arg.split_whitespace() {\n            if tok.is_empty() {\n                return Err(());\n            }\n            let negative = tok.as_bytes()[0] == b'-';\n            let positive = tok.as_bytes()[0] == b'+';\n            let digits = if negative || positive { &tok[1..] } else { tok };\n            if digits.is_empty() {\n                return Err(());\n            }\n            for c in digits.chars() {\n                if !c.is_ascii_digit() {\n                    return Err(());\n                }\n            }\n            if digits.len() > 10 {\n                return Err(());\n            }\n            let val: i64 = if negative {\n                let mut v: i64 = 0;\n                for c in digits.chars() {\n                    v = v * 10 + (c as i64 - '0' as i64);\n                }\n                -v\n            } else {\n                let mut v: i64 = 0;\n                for c in digits.chars() {\n                    v = v * 10 + (c as i64 - '0' as i64);\n                }\n                v\n            };\n            if val < i32::MIN as i64 || val > i32::MAX as i64 {\n                return Err(());\n            }\n            let n = val as i32;\n            for existing in nums.iter() {\n                if *existing == n {\n                    return Err(());\n                }\n            }\n            nums.push(n);\n        }\n    }\n    Ok(nums)\n}\n\nfn is_sorted(a: &[i32]) -> bool {\n    for i in 0..a.len().wrapping_sub(1) {\n        if a[i] > a[i + 1] {\n            return false;\n        }\n    }\n    true\n}\n\nfn find_min_idx(a: &[i32]) -> usize {\n    let mut mi = 0usize;\n    for i in 1..a.len() {\n        if a[i] < a[mi] {\n            mi = i;\n        }\n    }\n    mi\n}\n\nfn sort_three(a: &mut Vec<i32>) {\n    if a.len() <= 1 || is_sorted(a) {\n        return;\n    }\n    if a.len() == 2 {\n        println!(\"sa\");\n        a.swap(0, 1);\n        return;\n    }\n    let mx = if a[0] > a[1] && a[0] > a[2] {\n        0\n    } else if a[1] > a[0] && a[1] > a[2] {\n        1\n    } else {\n        2\n    };\n    if mx == 0 {\n        println!(\"ra\");\n        a.rotate_left(1);\n    } else if mx == 1 {\n        println!(\"rra\");\n        a.rotate_right(1);\n    }\n    if a[0] > a[1] {\n        println!(\"sa\");\n        a.swap(0, 1);\n    }\n}\n\nfn sort_five(a: &mut Vec<i32>, b: &mut Vec<i32>) {\n    while a.len() > 3 {\n        let mi = find_min_idx(a);\n        if mi == 0 {\n            println!(\"pb\");\n            let v = a.remove(0);\n            b.insert(0, v);\n        } else if mi <= a.len() / 2 {\n            for _ in 0..mi {\n                println!(\"ra\");\n                a.rotate_left(1);\n            }\n            println!(\"pb\");\n            let v = a.remove(0);\n            b.insert(0, v);\n        } else {\n            for _ in 0..(a.len() - mi) {\n                println!(\"rra\");\n                a.rotate_right(1);\n            }\n            println!(\"pb\");\n            let v = a.remove(0);\n            b.insert(0, v);\n        }\n    }\n    sort_three(a);\n    while !b.is_empty() {\n        println!(\"pa\");\n        let v = b.remove(0);\n        a.insert(0, v);\n    }\n}\n\nfn push_swap(a: &mut Vec<i32>) {\n    let n = a.len();\n    if n <= 1 || is_sorted(a) {\n        return;\n    }\n    if n <= 3 {\n        sort_three(a);\n        return;\n    }\n    if n <= 5 {\n        let mut b: Vec<i32> = Vec::new();\n        sort_five(a, &mut b);\n        return;\n    }\n    let mut b: Vec<i32> = Vec::new();\n    let k = if n <= 20 { 5 } else { 30 };\n    let mn = *a.iter().min().unwrap();\n    let mx = *a.iter().max().unwrap();\n    let range = mx as f64 - mn as f64;\n    let chunk_size = if k > 0 { range / k as f64 } else { range };\n    for c in 0..k {\n        let lo = mn as f64 + chunk_size * c as f64;\n        let hi = mn as f64 + chunk_size * (c + 1) as f64;\n        loop {\n            if a.is_empty() {\n                break;\n            }\n            let all_out = a.iter().all(|&v| (v as f64) < lo || (v as f64) > hi);\n            if all_out {\n                break;\n            }\n            let first = a[0] as f64;\n            if first >= lo && first <= hi {\n                println!(\"pb\");\n                let v = a.remove(0);\n                b.insert(0, v);\n            } else {\n                let mut best_pos = 0usize;\n                let mut best_is_top = true;\n                let mut found = false;\n                for i in 0..a.len() {\n                    let v = a[i] as f64;\n                    if v >= lo && v <= hi {\n                        let cost_top = i;\n                        let cost_bot = a.len() - i;\n                        if !found || cost_top < best_pos || (!best_is_top && cost_top <= best_pos) {\n                            best_pos = if cost_top <= cost_bot {\n                                best_is_top = true;\n                                cost_top\n                            } else {\n                                best_is_top = false;\n                                cost_bot\n                            };\n                            found = true;\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n                if !found {\n                    break;\n                }\n                if best_is_top {\n                    for _ in 0..best_pos {\n                        println!(\"ra\");\n                        a.rotate_left(1);\n                    }\n                } else {\n                    for _ in 0..best_pos {\n                        println!(\"rra\");\n                        a.rotate_right(1);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    while !b.is_empty() {\n        let mut max_idx = 0usize;\n        for i in 1..b.len() {\n            if b[i] > b[max_idx] {\n                max_idx = i;\n            }\n        }\n        let r = max_idx;\n        let rev = b.len() - max_idx;\n        if r == 0 {\n            println!(\"pa\");\n            let v = b.remove(0);\n            a.insert(0, v);\n        } else if r < rev {\n            for _ in 0..r {\n                println!(\"rb\");\n                b.rotate_left(1);\n            }\n            println!(\"pa\");\n            let v = b.remove(0);\n            a.insert(0, v);\n        } else {\n            for _ in 0..rev {\n                println!(\"rrb\");\n                b.rotate_right(1);\n            }\n            println!(\"pa\");\n            let v = b.remove(0);\n            a.insert(0, v);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nfn main() {\n    let args: Vec<String> = std::env::args().collect();\n    let nums = match parse_args(args) {\n        Ok(v) => v,\n        Err(()) => {\n            eprintln!(\"Error\");\n            std::process::exit(1);\n        }\n    };\n    if nums.is_empty() || is_sorted(&nums) {\n        return;\n    }\n    let mut a = nums;\n    let mut b: Vec<i32> = Vec::new();\n    let _ = &mut b;\n    push_swap(&mut a);\n}\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/work/push_swap.rs","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"work/push_swap.rs","time":{"start":1777738235970,"end":1777738235983}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The user wants me to implement the 42 push_swap project in Rust with specific constraints. Let me analyze the requirements:\n\n1. Single Rust source file `push_swap.rs` - no Cargo\n2. Must use only `rustc` with specific flags\n3. Two stacks (a and b), sort integers using specific operations\n4. Argument parsing rules\n5. Specific Makefile with targets: all, $(NAME), clean, fclean, re\n6. Restricted imports - only Vec, process::exit, env::args, println!, eprintln!, integer parsing\n\n\n7. No VecDeque, no Box, no Rc, no sort helpers, no unsafe\n8. Operation count grading bands\n\nNow I'm planning the implementation: I'll parse arguments handling both space-separated and quoted formats, validate for errors, then use a chunk-based sorting algorithm for larger inputs to stay within the operation limits. For the Makefile, I need to set up the standard targets with the rustc compilation command.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_de974c03d001z7ojgUaBh0Esyn","sessionID":"ses_2168e1f72ffejDHysUaUdBXqdN","messageID":"msg_de9745089001jLOwgk6gKK3tsw"}}
